1
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:45,230
Obsession can cause the unthinkable.

2
00:11:18,461 --> 00:11:24,461
Perfume: The Story of a Murderer is a crime, fantasy,
drama film directed by Tom Tykwer.

3
00:16:57,692 --> 00:17:03,692
Jean-Baptiste Grenouille, born in the stench of 18th century Paris, develops a superior
olfactory sense, which he uses to create the world's finest perfumes.

4
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:42,923
However, his work takes a dark turn as he tries to preserve
scents in the search for the ultimate perfume.

5
00:28:16,153 --> 00:28:22,153
Jean-Baptiste Grenouille, played by Ben Whishaw.

6
00:33:55,384 --> 00:34:01,384
Richis, played by Alan Rickman.

7
00:39:34,615 --> 00:39:40,615
Laura, played by Rachel Hurd-Wood.

8
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
Giuseppe Baldini, played by Dustin Hoffman.

9
00:50:53,076 --> 00:50:59,076
Narrator (voice), played by John Hurt.

10
00:56:32,307 --> 00:56:38,307
The Plum Girl, played by Karoline Herfurth.

11
01:02:11,538 --> 01:02:17,538
Perfume: The Story of a Murderer is a 2006 period psychological thriller film directed by Tom Tykwer, who cowrote the
screenplay with Andrew Birkin and Bernd Eichinger, based on the 1985 novel of the same name by Patrick Süskind.

12
01:07:50,769 --> 01:07:56,769
The film stars Ben Whishaw, Alan Rickman, Rachel Hurd-Wood and Dustin Hoffman.

13
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Set in 18th-century France, the film tells the story of Jean-Baptiste Grenouille
(Whishaw), an olfactory genius, and his homicidal quest for the perfect scent.

14
01:19:09,230 --> 01:19:15,230
Producer Eichinger bought the film rights to Süskind's novel in 2000,
and began writing the screenplay together with Birkin.

15
01:24:48,461 --> 01:24:54,461
Tykwer was selected as the director, and joined the two
in developing the screenplay in 2003.

16
01:30:27,692 --> 01:30:33,692
Principal photography began July 12, 2005, and concluded October 16, 2005.

17
01:36:06,923 --> 01:36:12,923
Filming took place in Spain, Germany and France.

18
01:41:46,153 --> 01:41:52,153
The film was made on a budget of €50 million (est.

19
01:47:25,384 --> 01:47:31,384
$60 million), making it one of the most expensive German films.

20
01:53:04,615 --> 01:53:10,615
A co-production of Germany, France, Spain and the United States, Perfume was released September 14, 2006, in Germany by Constantin Film,
December 26, 2006, in the United Kingdom by Pathé Distribution, and December 27, 2006, in the United States by DreamWorks Pictures.

21
01:58:43,846 --> 01:58:49,846
It grossed more than $135 million worldwide, of which
more than $53 million was made in Germany.

22
02:04:23,076 --> 02:04:29,076
Critics gave the film mixed reviews.

23
02:10:02,307 --> 02:10:08,307
The visual style and performances of Rickman and Whishaw were predominantly praised, while
the unevenness of the screenplay and casting of Hoffman were criticized.

24
02:15:41,538 --> 02:15:47,538
The film explores themes of daughter, small town,
bad smell, prostitute, paris, france.

25
02:21:20,769 --> 02:21:26,769
The tone is dark and emotional.
